c File: qg.order100.col
c 
c Source: Carla Gomes (gomes@cs.cornell.edu)
c 
c Description: This is an instance of the Quasigroup or  Latin Square Problem
c              (order 100). 
c              The problem corresponds to assigning colors to the 100 x 100 cells
c              of an empty matrix such there are no repetitions of colors
c              in each row/column of the matrix.
c
c Graph Structure: The graph has 10000 nodes and 990000 edges.
c Num. colors (optimal): 100
c
